title: Genesis 1 – The Creation
description: A verse-by-verse walk through Genesis 1: the six days of creation, the Word and Spirit at creation, and “Let us make man in our image.”
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-1-creation.html

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 1 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School · Genesis Series
sub: The Creation · Six Days · Very Good
refs: Genesis 1:1; Genesis 1:31
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The Foundation
--- In the Beginning
kicker: vv. 1–2 · The Foundation
scripture: Genesis 1:1-2 | mark: In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.; And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.

--- The Word & Spirit at Creation
kicker: Cross references · Genesis 1:1–2
xr: John 1:1-3 | The eternal Son, the Word, was present at and the active agent of all creation. “Without him was not any thing made” leaves no exception.
xr: Colossians 1:15-17 | Christ created all things and presently holds all things together. He is not just Creator, but Sustainer.
xr: Hebrews 1:1-3 | The Son is the exact image of God and the instrument through whom the worlds were made.

--- The Word & Spirit at Creation, continued
kicker: Cross references · Genesis 1:1–2
heading: The Word & Spirit at Creation
xr: Psalm 33:6 | Word and Breath (Spirit), both active in creation. Both present in Genesis 1:1–2 before a single creative act takes place.
callout: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit, all three present in the opening two verses of Scripture. The Bible does not begin with monotheism and slowly develop a Trinity. The Triune God is there from the very first word.

=== Days 1–3
--- Light
kicker: Day 1 · vv. 3–5
scripture: Genesis 1:3-5 | mark: And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.; God divided the light from the darkness.

--- The Firmament
kicker: Day 2 · vv. 6–8
scripture: Genesis 1:6-8 | mark: And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.

--- Land, Seas & Vegetation
kicker: Day 3 · vv. 9–13
scripture: Genesis 1:9-13 | mark: Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb yielding seed, and the fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, whose seed is in itself, upon the earth:

=== Days 4–5
--- Sun, Moon & Stars
kicker: Day 4 · vv. 14–19
scripture: Genesis 1:14-19 | mark: Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:; he made the stars also.

--- Fish & Fowl
kicker: Day 5 · vv. 20–23
scripture: Genesis 1:20-23 | mark: Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven.; Be fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let fowl multiply in the earth.

=== Day 6
--- Living Creatures
kicker: Day 6 · vv. 24–25 · The Crown of Creation
scripture: Genesis 1:24-25

--- Man, the Plural God Speaks
kicker: Day 6 · vv. 26–28
heading: Living Creatures & Man — The Plural God Speaks
scripture: Genesis 1:26-28 | mark: Let us make man in our image, after our likeness; So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.; Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it

--- Very Good
kicker: Day 6 · vv. 29–31
scripture: Genesis 1:29-30
big: Genesis 1:31 | mark: And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good.

--- Jesus in Genesis 1
kicker: Cross references · Genesis 1:26
heading: Jesus in Genesis 1 — “Let Us Make Man in Our Image”
xr: Genesis 1:26 | **The Plural.** “Us / Our”: God speaks in the plural within Himself. Man is made in God’s image, not angels’. This cannot be God addressing angels. This is the Triune God deliberating within Himself.
xr: John 1:1 | **John 1:1, 14.** The One who said “Let us make man in our image” later became the Man, taking on the very nature He designed. [[John 1:14]]
xr: Colossians 1:15-16 | Man was created by Christ and for Christ. The Creator later became the Redeemer of what He made.

--- Jesus in Genesis 1, continued
kicker: Cross references · Genesis 1:26
heading: Jesus in Genesis 1 — “Let Us Make Man in Our Image”
xr: Proverbs 8:22-30 | Wisdom personified, present with God at creation, rejoicing. A picture of the pre-incarnate Son (cf. [[1 Corinthians 1:24|1 Cor. 1:24]], [[1 Corinthians 1:30|30]]).
xr: Hebrews 1:10 | Quoting [[Psalm 102:25]]. The writer of Hebrews quotes Psalm 102 and applies it directly to the Son. The Father calls Christ the Creator of heaven and earth.
xr: 1 Corinthians 8:6 | “By whom are all things, and we by him.” Paul includes our very existence as coming through Christ the Creator.

--- Creation and redemption
kicker: Cross references · Genesis 1:26
heading: Creation and Redemption
callout: “Let us make man” is not a detail to pass over. The Son who spoke those words in eternity past is the same Son who took on that image in Bethlehem ([[Philippians 2:7|Phil. 2:7]]), died for those who bore it, and will one day present a redeemed humanity perfectly conformed to His own glorious image ([[Romans 8:29|Rom. 8:29]]). Creation and redemption are one unbroken story.

=== Day 7
--- God Rested, Sanctified the Seventh Day
kicker: Day 7 · Genesis 2:1–3 · The Sabbath
scripture: Genesis 2:1-3 | mark: God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.; And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it:
